   "k": "j6k4di",
   "en": "Strategies and guides"
  },
  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "6vskcs",
   "en": "Shanxi starts off with 2 debuffs on political power and stability. Choose Secure Internal Politics to get a fascist demagogue and complete Industrial Investment, Local Arms Production, Public Education Reform and finally Opposition before fire off a civil war."
  },
  {
   "k": "7ed9py",
   "en": "Keep training your starting army until you get 5 Army EXP to make a cavalry unit. To prepare for civil war, queue a cavalry division and remember to lower your stability from time to time with the decision to Commandeer Civilian Trains (research civilian train beforehand) and Prepare for Civil War. Delete your starting army before the civil war."
  },
  {
   "k": "b5358f",
   "en": "When the civil war has started, force deploy the cavalry unit to start capturing victory point and after the civil war, you're now fascist with no debuffs spirit. Then, you have to join Japan's faction once its available and build yourself up for the border wars without any threats from anyone, just don't join Japan's war. Focus on the other warlords' territories like Xibei San Ma and Sinkiang since the supply is horrendous there. Your faction members will flood their army in so turn off the supply sharing to only supply yourself."
  },
  {
   "k": "1cqv17y",
   "en": "As for the border conflict template, 6 divisions of 7-2 (7 infantry and 2 artillery with 1 support artillery) is good enough with your limited industry. Research mountaineer is a good start as well. If you have extra military factories, you might want to add in support artillery, medium flame tank, engineer, radio and recon company. Don't border war with Communist China and Nationalist China initially. To win the border war with Communist China, you have to place your army at Ordos border with Shaanxi which controlled by Communist China to start the conflict."
  },
  {
   "k": "x4kcgg",
   "en": "When you get enough land, industry and army, you can consider to leave Japan's faction and let them declare war on you since they have a wargoal on you that stays with them even after they lost to the Allies."
  },
  {
   "k": "1ncb2jm",
   "en": "There are 2 focus you can get in the end of Opposition path: Nationalist or Communist. If you decide to go for Nationalist China focus tree, immediately Invite Foreign Investor and rush down all the focus on the German side to get the buffs for your army and extra military factories. With that, you can build up even stronger than before. Then, the future of Shanxi is depends on your choice."
  },
  {
   "k": "1nu7ub0",
   "en": "However, if you decided to go for Communist China focus tree, kick out the fascist demagogue during civil war. Wait till you get enough PP to get a Communist Revolutionary and flip to Communist as Shanxi Soviet Republic. You have to wait till your Communist ideology reaches 50% to get the Communist focus tree in Proclaim The Rival Government. Then you have to rush Social Democracy path to annex China peacefully, collect all their troops and prepare to rush down Guangxi Clique as they are the faction leader. Since you're in Japan's faction, they will give you back your core territories. If everything is done right, the China War should end in 1940 and you have time to prep yourself before leaving the faction and let Japan declare war on you."
  },
  {
   "k": "15bpiaj",
   "en": "Alternately, you can hire a fascist demagogue after Secure Internal Politics and remove your debuffs in Cooperation with the Nationalist. You need to keep increasing the fascist ideology through decision and events to hopefully turn fascist before the China War, stop taking any focus to gain more Political Power if necessary. After joined Japan's faction, do the same thing by annex China peacefully, rush down Guangxi and reclaim all of China."
  },
